const __JAGR='\n\nTHE JUDGES\' AGREEMENT (what you enforce; not your posture). The judges whose lines you check accepted the text below before the debate was judged. It binds them; it does not make you a judge, and the instruction above stands.\n\n'+"You are an adjudicator of a debate record. You decide which side the verses in the record support, under the rules you are given. You bring nothing from outside the record. You are deciding what each side established in the record, under the rules you are given.\n\n### Commitment 1. The record is the only evidence.\nThe evidence is the rounds of both sides. The system also serves you the KJV citation report, the pressed-witness ledger and the challenger link numbers; these report on the rounds and are part of the record. The pre-checks are aids that decide nothing. Your own knowledge, from training or anywhere else, is not evidence: it does not raise or lower any argument, settle any disputed point, or supply any missing step.\n\n### Commitment 2. I repair nothing.\nYou supply no missing step for either side. A debater's inference, exhibited in the record with its footing, is evidence: an [L4] stands when it exhibits at least two lower layers ([L1] KJV text, [L2] Hebrew or Greek word, [L3] cross-reference) and the chain from them, and falls when it does not. Any inference of your own shows two lower layers, as a debater's must.\n\n### Commitment 3. Meaning, not words.\nScripture does not contradict itself. If a debater's link cannot agree with the meaning of a verse pressed against it, as the debaters show that meaning with its layers, the link fails: the verse stands, and the link is the error. You weigh only the meaning the debaters show, and add none of your own. The wording of one verse alone never decides a link, and no side may demand that one verse state the point: \"no verse states it\", \"the text nowhere narrates it\" and \"no witness's own words state it\" are never a ground, for either side. Scripture is read precept upon precept (Isaiah 28:10): \"scripture, read precept upon precept, does not give [the fact]\" is a ground when it names the fact and exhibits the scripture that does speak to it, one verse or many read together, precept upon precept; no count of verses decides it.\n\n### Commitment 4. One standard for both sides.\nThe same evidentiary, logical and answering threshold applies to both sides, whatever the position, its popularity, or its agreement with consensus. No side receives heightened scrutiny. A test you apply to one side's link you apply to the other side's link on the same collision line.\n\n### Commitment 5. Silence is not neutral.\nA proven press carried under a listed premise's PRESSED WITH line (one that carries its layers, or a checked reference to the round that shows them), and left unanswered by the later rounds of the side that holds the link, makes that premise UNEXHIBITED. It is not missing information; it is a failure to respond that the record shows. A press without its proof is not a witness, and leaving it unanswered costs nothing. A verse pressed with no listed premise behind it is not a witness. A premise carries at most eight witnesses.\n\n### Commitment 6. I void only by quoting.\nYou rule a listed premise VOID only by quoting the words of its charge that go beyond its quote, and naming the kind: a negation, a universal, or a claim the quote's own words do not make. Paraphrase, reordering and dropped words are not stronger. A charge written as ASSUMES: ... -- ROWS GIVE: ... is never voided for its words; you check it against the rows (ruling 421).\n\n### Commitment 7. I judge; I do not only count.\nAt each collision point I decide which link the pressed verses agree with. I read the meaning each side showed for each verse pressed there, set both links against those verses, and rule: a link that cannot agree with a pressed verse's meaning fails (Commitment 3); a link that agrees with all of them stands. Where the sides show different meanings for one verse, I rule which shown meaning the verse's own layers support (its words, the lexicon line quoted whole, its cross-references), and I quote them; a meaning shown by cutting a lexicon line fails. A collision is UNDERDETERMINED only when, after that weighing, both links agree with every pressed verse's meaning, and I then quote the words of the verse each link agrees with. That a side answered is not a ground; an answer is weighed for whether it shows the fit, not counted because it was given. My rulings show two lower layers, as Commitment 2 requires. My count of premises follows from these rulings and does not replace them.\n\n### Commitment 8. The method is Isaiah 28:10.\nThe method. Isaiah 28:10 (KJV): \"For precept must be upon precept, precept upon precept; line upon line, line upon line; here a little, and there a little:\" The case is not one verse; it is verses laid on verses until the point stands. That is how these debates are built and how they are judged.\n- [L1] The KJV verse: the verse itself, quoted exactly.\n- [L2] Source language: the Hebrew or Greek behind the English.\n- [L3] Cross-reference: what the rest of scripture says.\n- [L4] Inference: a conclusion the debater draws from at least two prior layers.\nHow the case is judged. To win, the challenger must break the defender's chain, the linked argument the defender builds for the topic. Defeating one isolated verse or term does not break the chain. A chain breaks in one of two ways: the challenger shows that a link cannot agree with the meaning of a verse pressed against it, as the debaters show that meaning with its layers, and the defender shows no fit (Commitment 3); or the defender takes down enough of its own links.\n\n### Commitment 9. I answer in the form each request gives.\nMy judgment is the strict JSON the system message gives, and nothing else. A request that is not for my judgment, such as a cure request or a line an enforcer sends back to me, is answered only in the plain lines that request gives, one per item, and never in JSON. When an enforcer sends a line of mine back with its reason, I answer every item it sends: I keep my line or change it, and I quote the debate's own words that decide it.\n\n### Commitment 10. I capture contradictions.\nBefore my verdict, I list every place where a side asserts in a later round what it withdrew or conceded in an earlier round, and every place where a side states two things that cannot both be true. I write these lines inside my \"reasoning\", one line for each:\nCONTRADICTION -- <side> -- EARLIER (<round>, \"<quote>\") -- LATER (<round>, \"<quote>\")\nIf the engine marks a contradiction that I judge is not one, I write:\nNOT HELD -- <mark> -- \"<quote>\" -- <why, from the text>\nIf I find none, I write: CONTRADICTIONS: NONE FOUND.\nFor every withdrawal or concession the engine puts to me (K-W), I answer in one of three forms: STANDS WITHOUT IT because <layer>; CONCEDED; or REASSERTED IN <round> \"<quote>\", when a later round rests on what was withdrawn.\nEvery quote must stand in its round text. A contradiction the engine found that I neither list nor answer NOT HELD is recorded against my seat. So is NONE FOUND written where the engine found one."; // package C (operator 2026-11-05 18:05 CST: the enforcer needs to know what to enforce on that judge)
// ruling 428 step 3 (K-W): the test is whether the judge's named layer carries the fact the withdrawn sentence carried, while the side still claims it
// (run 32677: three judges stood D5 on Galatians 4:4 after the Mary-flesh sentence was withdrawn; the dry re-grade 32686 enforcer said NEEDS: NO).
// ruling 421 (#1 and #4; TRIAL; md_notes_rulings 421: "remove deepseek as a judge and debator and make it a default enforcer"): the DeepSeek enforcer.
// Code found each item (K-W: a side's own withdrawal or grant; K-S3: a close-round concession not marked COUNTED), each panel judge answered it in
// its cure (Panel Cure Check, enforcer_log rows), and here one DeepSeek call checks every answer against the round words. TRIAL: its verdicts are
// recorded in debate_enforcer_log (kind enforcer_check) and remove no seat. Items are grouped by the side's sentence, so a round excerpt is sent once.
const PCC=$('Panel Cure Check').first().json;const S=$('Init Seats').first().json;let RS=null;try{RS=$('Resolve Seats').first().json;}catch(e){RS=null;}
const rows=(PCC.enforcer_log||[]).filter(r=>r&&(r.rule==='K-W'||r.rule==='K-S3'));
const ds=RS&&RS.deepseek&&RS.deepseek.api_model?RS.deepseek:null;
if(!rows.length||!ds)return [{json:{enf_skip:true,why:!rows.length?'no K-W or K-S3 item was asked':'no DeepSeek model_config row'}}];
let R=null;for(const n of ['Panel Cure Normalize 1','Panel Cure Normalize 2','Panel Cure Normalize 3']){try{if($(n).isExecuted)for(const it of $(n).all()){const c=it.json&&it.json.cure;if(c&&c.rounds){R=c.rounds;break;}}}catch(e){}if(R)break;}
const clean=s=>String(s||'').replace(/[*_`]+/g,'');
const sentOf=r=>{const l=String(r.flagged_line||'');if(r.rule==='K-W'){const m=l.match(/:\s*"([\s\S]*)"\s*$/);return m?m[1]:l;}const m=l.match(/^(?:DEFENDER|CHALLENGER)\s+(?:CR|DR)[1-4]\s*:?\s*([\s\S]*)$/i);return m?m[1]:l;};
const rkOf=r=>((String(r.item||'')+' '+String(r.flagged_line||'')).match(/\b((?:CR|DR)[1-4])\b/)||[])[1]||null;
const nzd=s=>clean(s).normalize('NFD').replace(/[\u0300-\u036f]/g,'').replace(/["\u201c\u201d\u2018\u2019']/g,'').replace(/\s+/g,' '); /* run 32662: a judge wrote "ginosko" for the round's "ginōskō" and dropped the marks around "only"; accents, quotation marks and spacing are not read */
// ruling 424 (run 32677): the enforcer reads the link's own blocks from every round of the side that holds it, not a window around the sentence.
const HD=/(?:^|\n)[ \t>#*-]*((?:LINK\s*\d+|[DC]\d+)\b[^\n:]{0,60}):/gi;
const blocksOf=t=>{t=clean(t);const hs=[...t.matchAll(HD)].map(m=>({at:m.index,lab:m[1]}));return hs.map((h,k)=>({lab:h.lab,text:t.slice(h.at,k+1<hs.length?hs[k+1].at:t.length).trim()}));};
const tokOf=lab=>{const m=String(lab||'').match(/LINK\s*\d+|\b[DC]\d+\b/i);return m?m[0].replace(/\s+/g,' ').toUpperCase():null;};
const SIDE_RK={CR:['CR1','CR2','CR3','CR4'],DR:['DR1','DR2','DR3','DR4']};
const cut=(s,n)=>{s=String(s||'');return s.length>n?s.slice(0,n)+' [...]':s;};
const excerpt=(rk,s,lab)=>{if(!R||!rk)return '(round text not available)';const fam=rk.slice(0,2);const tok=tokOf(lab);const key=nzd(s).slice(0,60),key2=nzd(s).slice(0,30);const parts=[];let own=null;
 for(const r of SIDE_RK[fam]){const t=R[r];if(!t)continue;
  if(r.endsWith('1')){if(tok){const rx=new RegExp('\\b'+tok.replace(' ','\\s*')+'\\b','i');const ls=clean(t).split('\n').filter(l=>rx.test(l)).slice(0,4);if(ls.length)parts.push('['+r+'] '+ls.map(l=>cut(l,500)).join(' / '));}continue;}
  for(const b of blocksOf(t)){const bt=tokOf(b.lab);const mine=!!tok&&bt===tok;const nb=nzd(b.text);const hasS=nb.includes(key)||(!!key2&&nb.includes(key2));
   if(r===rk&&hasS&&(mine||!own))own={r,b,mine};if(mine)parts.push('['+r+'] '+cut(b.text,3500));}}
 if(!own){const k=nzd(R[rk]||'').indexOf(key);if(k<0)parts.unshift('(the sentence was not found in ['+rk+'])');}
 else if(!own.mine)parts.unshift('['+own.r+'] (the block holding the sentence) '+cut(own.b.text,3500));
 return cut(parts.join('\n\n'),9000)||'(no block of this link found)';};
const G=[];const key=r=>r.rule+'|'+String(r.item||'').replace(/\s*#\d+$/,'')+'|'+clean(sentOf(r)).slice(0,120); /* ruling 424: "I grant that." under D3 and under D5 are two items */
for(const r of rows){let g=G.find(x=>x.key===key(r));if(!g){g={key:key(r),rule:r.rule,rk:rkOf(r),sent:sentOf(r),item:r.item,lab:(String(r.item||'').match(/(?:CR|DR)[1-4]\s+(.+?)\s+#\d+$/)||[])[1]||null,ans:[]};G.push(g);}g.ans.push(r);}
const ids=[];const parts=G.map((g,k)=>{const lines=g.ans.map((r,j)=>{const id='A'+(k+1)+'.'+(j+1);ids.push({id,row:r});return '- '+id+' ('+r.seat+'): '+(r.response_line?String(r.response_line).replace(/\s+/g,' ').slice(0,700):'none written');});
 return 'ITEM G'+(k+1)+' ('+g.rule+', '+g.item+'):\nTHE SIDE\'S SENTENCE: "'+String(g.sent).slice(0,300)+'"\nTHE SIDE\'S OWN BLOCKS FOR THIS LINK, FROM EVERY ROUND OF THAT SIDE:\n'+excerpt(g.rk,g.sent,g.lab)+'\nTHE JUDGES\' ANSWERS:\n'+lines.join('\n');});
const SYS='You are the enforcer of a debate panel. You check the judges\' written answers against the debate round words quoted to you. You bring nothing from outside the record: no doctrine, no training knowledge, no reading of your own. You check only whether each answer agrees with the quoted round words. You do not judge the debate.';
const RULES='RULE K-W (a side withdrew or granted, in its own round, footing of a link it keeps). A judge answers STANDS WITHOUT IT because <a layer>, or CONCEDED. Decide FIRST, from the side\'s own blocks given you: what fact did the withdrawn or granted sentence carry for this link (a descent, a source, a time, a person)? Does the side, anywhere in its blocks for this link, still claim that same fact? If it still claims it, STANDS WITHOUT IT is right only when the layer the judge names carries that same fact in its own words; if the named layer does not carry it, the right answer is CONCEDED: AGREE with CONCEDED and DISAGREE with STANDS WITHOUT IT. If the side no longer claims the fact, STANDS WITHOUT IT is right: AGREE when the layer the judge names is footing the side itself gives this link, and DISAGREE when the judge supplies footing the side never gave. Write NEEDS: YES when the side still claims the withdrawn fact, NEEDS: NO when it does not. A verse missing from the blocks given you is not, by that alone, a reason to disagree: read the meaning the side shows.\n'
 +'RULE K-S3 (a close-round concession the judge\'s count did not mark COUNTED). A judge answers COUNTED, or TOUCHES NO LINK: <why>. Decide FIRST: does the concession give up part of a declared link or of a listed premise? If it does, AGREE with COUNTED and DISAGREE with TOUCHES NO LINK; if it does not, the reverse.\n'
 +'An answer that is missing, or in neither form: NO ANSWER.\n'
 +'Reply with exactly one line per answer id, and nothing else, in this form:\nENFORCER: <answer id> -- AGREE | DISAGREE | NO ANSWER -- NEEDS: YES | NO -- <one sentence that quotes the side\'s words that decide it>';
const USER=RULES+'\n\n'+parts.join('\n\n');
const body={model:ds.api_model,max_tokens:Math.max(Number(ds.max_tokens)||0,16000),temperature:0,messages:[{role:'system',content:SYS+__JAGR},{role:'user',content:USER}]};
return [{json:{enf_skip:false,body,ids:ids.map(x=>({id:x.id,seat:x.row.seat,seat_role:x.row.seat_role,rule:x.row.rule,item:x.row.item,flagged_line:x.row.flagged_line,response_line:x.row.response_line,cure_status:x.row.cure_status})),groups:G.length,model:ds.api_model,run_token:S.run_token}}];
